  "query_preview": "..\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW:\nThere is a surface front that is moving through the area. This has\nhelped advect some higher dew point air into the eastern half of\nthe area. This upslope flow may be enough to initiate an isolated\nstorm in the east from 4 PM to 8 PM this evening. A cold front is\nexpected to move in from the north and have gusty winds with it,\nso area lakes will be more difficult to navigate this evening into\nthe overnight. There is also potential for haze from wildfire\nsmoke and impacts to those with breathing challenges from 6 PM to\n4 AM in the morning. There is decent uncertainty for convection \ntomorrow afternoon, but the most likely place for storms is in the\neastern half of the area from 5 PM to midnight. \n\nAfter Monday evening, an active pattern looks like it will move in\nfor a multiple days. Temperatures are expected to be around\naverage for Tuesday and Wednesday. For Thursday through Saturday,\nthe GFS and ECMWF ensembles indicate high temperatures being the\n60s and 70s. Part of the story is the shower and thunderstorm\nchances returning for the area. The ensemble are indicating some\nmonsoonal moisture will make its way into Montana from the\nsouthwest U.S.. With dry conditions ahead of this activity, fire \nstarts are one of the possibilities. The GFS does not bring a high\nlevel of CAPE on Wednesday through Saturday, which basically \nmeans there is high uncertainty around thunderstorm strength.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\nIncreased PoPs slightly in the east to cover Sidney Airport and\nother areas of Richland County. Used the HRW FV3 to adjust winds\nto align with the cold frontal passage this evening. No other\nadjustments were made.\n\nThere is moderate to high confidence in the Lake Wind Advisory for\ntonight, and similar confidence in the timing and placement of\nhaze according to the 12Z HRRR model.\n\nThere is low confidence in thunderstorms occurring in the east\ntonight, and low to moderate confidence for tomorrow evening.\n\nThere is high confidence in temperatures cooling down a bit\nstarting on Thursday.",
